  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved working conditions and protection from unacceptable forms of work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Serbia&apos;s new Law on Occupational Safety and Health (OSH), adopted in April 2023, lays the foundation for modernizing the OSH recording, reporting, and notification system. Its full implementation will be supported by a forthcoming Law on Occupational Injuries and Diseases Insurance and additional secondary legislation. 
Aligned with the EU OSH Framework Directive (89/391 EEC), the law prioritizes risk prevention, workplace safety, hazard elimination, and improved worker participation and training. Under the Safety + Health for All program, the ILO provides technical support in drafting the new insurance law, assessing OSH services&apos; alignment with international standards, and modernizing OSHD&#x2019;s internal training capacities. Additionally, the ILO addresses the outdated, paper-based registration system for licensing OSH professionals.</narrative>
  </description>
